Z||000000||AkursedX||05-24-2001||08:57 PM||||Does anyone have a picture of '88 GT wheels on an 84-87 Coupe or GT?  <BR>Or does anyone have this done?  What does it look like?  Is the offset really noticable?<P>The reason I am asking is because I should be getting and 86 coupe very soon, and I have my 88GT rims just lying around so I figure I would like to put them to some good use, but I'm curious to see what it would look like 1st.  I hope I'll be able to do it.  Having those 88GT rims just sitting around is such a waste  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fformula88||05-24-2001||09:37 PM||||I put up my sig 'cause the Formula is the same body style as an 87 coupe.  I wouldn't think the difference in offset is so great that it will cause a big problem or a highly noticeable difference.  The rims are so close that the idiots at the Dunn Tire on Walden managed to put the the bigger (215/60) on the smaller "front" rims and the 205/60's on the bigger rear rims, then procede to mount them on the wrong ends of the car!  LOL.  They were really ticked off too when I told them they had to be re-mounted the correct way.  So I am guessing they won't look out of place on a non 88.  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||05-24-2001||10:11 PM||||They won't look out of place at all.  It's just when you put pre-88 GT wheels on '88s the front tire will stick out of the wheel well, noticeable, and nasty IMHO.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||05-24-2001||11:15 PM||||I have three 86-87 gt rims. If you bought them you would have a set for your car,||||reg||1
Z||000004||FierobearRoadtrip||05-26-2001||02:46 PM||||I put 88 Formula (same as GT) rims on my wife's 86 coupe. I think it improved the ride and handling, but then there were crappy aftermarket rims on there before. They look really nice, too.||||reg||1
